  "content_blocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "This section helps to\ndesign web banners\nin the Bosch Corporate Design. To fully implement the designs, a basic understanding of the Core and the general design principles of the Digital Design System is required:\nSee general design principles"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The web banner layout is based on a predefined baseline grid and a variable column grid. This allows a flexible component placement while keeping consistent spacings."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Baseline grid and padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Baseline grid:\nAll components are aligned along a square 0.25 rem (4 px) baseline grid. The spacing between each line can be easily defined in increments of rem (0.5 rem, 1 rem, 2 rem, 3 rem).\nPadding:\nHorizontal and vertical spacing within the Brand Area, i.e. between supergraphic bar, symbol/logotype and content, as well as from content to Experience Area (product image). Padding depends on the web banner size, the structure within the brand/experience layer as well as the content density."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The Bosch Digital Design System provides predefined spacing throughout components and also between the components for easier layout work.\nLearn more on general spacing"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Spacings within a template"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Banners are following the Bosch Layout Principle consisting of two flexible areas:\nBrand Area:\nThe Brand Area offers room for the Bosch Brand and always contains at least the Supergraphic, symbol / logotype and slogan.\nExperience Area:\nThe Experience Area contains images, colors or illustrations."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The Bosch Layout Principle for web banners\nThe versatility of the Bosch Layout Principle has been optimized for the small space offered in banners. The goal is to achieve good legibility on the small surface area within the image section.\nTherefore, specific rules apply here:\nThe text can be placed either on the Brand Area or within an additional content tile on Experience Area.\nThe text may not be placed without a tile (on the Experience Area).\nThe placement and size of Supergraphic and Symbol / logotype is predefined within the web banner template and must not be changed.\nFurthermore, the existing rules still apply:\nThe relation between the Brand Area and the Experience Area is flexible; an image can be enlarged or minimized depending on the amount of text (rolling shutter principle).\nThe placement of Supergraphic and Symbol / logotype can be varied in the web banner template – top, bottom or left, right.\nIn addition, a solid filled tile can be placed on the experience area to show text.\nOnly one button may be used as a call-to-action on Primary Background.\nOn Major Highlight Background, no button may be used. Instead, a pseudo headline link is mandatory. More info can be found\nhere\n.\nMandatory elements\nHeadline, symbol / logotype & Primary Button (or Headline link)\nOptional elements\nSubline, bold copy & image"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Billboard: 93.75 × 43.75 rem (1500 × 700 px)\nHalfpage Ad: 18.75 × 37.5 rem (300 × 600 px)\nMedium Rectangle: 18.75 × 15.625 rem (300 × 250 px)\nSkyscraper: 10 × 37.5 rem (160 × 600 px)\nWide Leaderboard: 60.625 × 5.625 rem (970 × 90 px)"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Special button types are used for the banner design. These are conditioned on the one hand, by the smaller design area and on the other hand, in combination with the adjacent content (headline, subline) to create a balanced overall picture.\nThese differ from the standard core button in the height and the distances before and after the text label."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Button Large"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Button Small"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "References"
    },
    {
